    <briefdescription>
<para>Comparator that orders indices into the current GB array (<computeroutput><ref refid="f4-types_8hpp_a2e9f3698c99ce95a0e99361e755bce3c_1a2e9f3698c99ce95a0e99361e755bce3c" kindref="member">gb_array</ref></computeroutput>) by each <computeroutput><ref refid="structgbelem" kindref="compound">gbelem</ref></computeroutput>&apos;s leading monomial, in increasing order. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>operator()</computeroutput> returns true when <computeroutput><ref refid="class_g_b_sorter_a68f7f6c3a4cb24ad42e2811cc90301a9_1a68f7f6c3a4cb24ad42e2811cc90301a9" kindref="member">gb</ref>[a]</computeroutput>&apos;s leading monomial is strictly less than <computeroutput><ref refid="class_g_b_sorter_a68f7f6c3a4cb24ad42e2811cc90301a9_1a68f7f6c3a4cb24ad42e2811cc90301a9" kindref="member">gb</ref>[b]</computeroutput>&apos;s under <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_info_a0d39f02d353521b5d8eafc1caf2d63e2_1a0d39f02d353521b5d8eafc1caf2d63e2" kindref="member">MonomialInfo::compare</ref></computeroutput>. Like <computeroutput><ref refid="class_columns_sorter" kindref="compound">ColumnsSorter</ref></computeroutput> it keeps <computeroutput><ref refid="class_g_b_sorter_ac73cfe8e093af9de81aa3e229158c44e_1ac73cfe8e093af9de81aa3e229158c44e" kindref="member">ncmps</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_g_b_sorter_a9bc7d687dfacb8aa524f83b98c58f7f1_1a9bc7d687dfacb8aa524f83b98c58f7f1" kindref="member">ncmps0</ref></computeroutput> profiling counters. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
